# The specialized version of a loop reads its array through the storage that was read before its iterations. In a user's build no iteration checks whether the array has changed.
# Everything depends on two things: the iteration exits to the generic version before an operation that may move the storage, and what the iterations do is recorded.
# Fault injection, testing=IgnoreLoopArrayStores: an iteration of a specialized version does not exit at a store into an array, and the trial visits do not record the store.
# The store itself is still built, and it invalidates what it writes.
# The callback of filter appends eight elements to the array that is being filtered, which moves that array's storage, and then stores to an element further ahead.
# With only the fault injected, filter keeps reading the old storage and misses what was stored: a silently wrong result.
# With --aot-harden=ignore-told-ranges (testing=CheckBoundsAtRunTime) and with proof-checks (testing=CheckProofsAtRunTime) the emitter checks the storage in every iteration.
# It compares the storage with a fresh read from the array, and the process crashes with a named error.
# The second function stores to an element further ahead and moves nothing, so its result is right with the fault injected too.
# RUN(RIGHT): run-in-shell mechanisms=all testing=CheckBoundsAtRunTime
# RIGHT: 5:1,3,5,101,7, 16 5:1,3,5,101,7, 8
# RIGHT-NEXT: exited with 0
# RUN(UNHELD): run-in-shell mechanisms=all testing=IgnoreLoopArrayStores
# UNHELD: 5:1,3,5,101,7, 9 5:1,3,5,101,7, 8
# UNHELD-NEXT: exited with 0
# RUN(HELD): run-in-shell mechanisms=all testing=IgnoreLoopArrayStores,CheckBoundsAtRunTime
# HELD: bun: internal AOT error:
# HELD: crashed with SIGABRT
# RUN(PROOFS): run-in-shell mechanisms=all testing=IgnoreLoopArrayStores,CheckProofsAtRunTime
# PROOFS: bun: internal AOT error:
# PROOFS: crashed with SIGABRT
